Is their any documentation on that yet ?

@therne any chance to have it on Linux? :)

Wow, that's too much responsibilities we give to bots. How can we be sure they don't abuse access? For example, can we confirm their actions?

@busmark\_w\_nika Yes, we have a/ permission level control, and b/ Final confirm. so Aside will ask before crucial actions like send, pay, delete, or submit.

I'm on Dia right now and I'd be hard-put to swap (took me ages to move from Arc), but the logged-in account part is the piece Dia doesn't touch. What does that get me that a sidebar doesn't and how do you guys handle profiles (The swiping between profiles is the big reason I'm a DIA/Arc guy) [...] @justin\_rockmore We also support swiping profiles, but it is strongly binded to Aside account. But the good news is, we'll support Arc/Dia like profile system in 1-2 week!

@chanhee Awesome - so to clarify I'd need 1 Aside account currently or, in this particular use case, I'd need 3-4 (one per profile). [...] There's nothing else doing it the way Aside is and I look forward to seeing it grow as time goes on! Just hoping it doesn't pull a BCoNY on us 😉

@sammykins I saw your comment on X and share it to the team. Looking into it!

Been using Aside as my daily browser for about a month now, and out of every AI browser I've tried, this is the one that stuck.

Two things sold me.

First, context. You can connect your existing AI subscriptions or API access, or just use the connection Aside gives you. But the part other browsers miss is that your context actually comes with you. No re-prompting, no exporting a chat to paste somewhere else. It's just there.Second, the AI is opt-in. This works as both a browser and a space for your AI chats, so nothing gets summarized unless I ask for it.
